card.statement:
Let $h\mapsto \hat h$ be an involutive automorphism of the skew field of quaternions.
The quaternion matrix equation
${AX-\widehat XB=C}$ has a solution if and only if

\begin{equation}
\widehat S^{-1}\begin{bmatrix}
A&C\\0&B
\end{bmatrix}S= \begin{bmatrix}
A&0\\0&B
\end{bmatrix}
\end{equation}

for some nonsingular $S$.
